.TH ARGUS-GUI 1 "2026-11-27" "argus 1.5.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
argus-gui \- desktop front-end for the argus security scanner
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B argus-gui
.RB [ \-\-tk ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B argus-gui
starts the desktop front-end shipped with
.BR argus (1).
It can start a scan, browse findings, filter and sort results, inspect
dependency trees and compare two JSON reports.
.PP
The window is built with Qt (PySide6).  When
.B PySide6
is not installed for the current interpreter, the Tk front-end is used
instead, so the command keeps working on systems without Qt.
The Debian package installs PySide6 into its private runtime
.I /var/lib/argus-scanner/runtime
during installation.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-tk
Force the Tk front-end even when Qt is available.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DISPLAY
X11 display used by both front-ends.
.TP
.B WAYLAND_DISPLAY
Wayland display; Qt selects the Wayland platform when available.
.TP
.B QT_QPA_PLATFORM
Qt platform plugin, for example
.I offscreen
for automated screenshots.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR argus (1),
.BR argus-setup-runtime (1),
.I /usr/share/doc/argus-scanner/README.md
.SH AUTHOR
argus contributors.
